ed directive `//go:embed templates/skills` embeds the whole directory. If a file inside is deleted, the embed still works (embeds whatever's there). It will NOT fail — embed.FS with directory pattern embeds the tree, and missing files just aren't there. The build succeeds, just without grilling.md content.\n\nWait, but is that right? Let me verify: `//go:embed templates/skills` — this embeds the directory `templates/skills` recursively. If we delete one file inside, the directory still exists and the embed succeeds with remaining files. Yes. Build succeeds.\n\nLet me verify this claim quickly by testing: temporarily rename grilling.md, go build, then restore. Actually, I shouldn't mutate the repo during test generation investigation too casually, but I can do it in a safe way (backup and restore). Let me verify the go:embed behavior to be confident.\n\nActually, let me just verify carefully with a safe test.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_5vSqr36fxK6PPRUZRtU47085","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && cp internal/prompt/templates/skills/grilling.md /tmp/grilling.md.bak && rm internal/prompt/templates/skills/grilling.md && echo \"deleted, now build:\" && tmp=$(mktemp -d) && go build -o \"$tmp/rick\" ./cmd/rick 2>&1; echo \"build exit=$?\"; ls \"$tmp/rick\" 2>/dev/null && echo \"binary produced\"; mv /tmp/grilling.md.bak internal/prompt/templates/skills/grilling.md && echo \"restored\"; ls internal/prompt/templates/skills/grilling.md && rm -rf \"$tmp\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":109,"output":3353,"cacheRead":56704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3151,"totalTokens":60166,"cost":{"input":0.000047415,"output":0.00291711,"cacheRead":0.000205552,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.003170077}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913610468,"responseId":"930b96d2-99d6-4a4a-8bd6-9d129f8e75fd","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"