after task10, since grilling present = normal path succeeds). If this fails, it indicates either the probe is broken or BuildPlan has a bug independent of grilling deletion. This is a legitimate check. I'll include it but make the error message clear.\n\nWait, but is it guaranteed that after task10, BuildPlan with grilling present returns NO_ERROR? Yes — the whole point is that with grilling present, BuildPlan succeeds (inlines it). So NO_ERROR is correct. And before task10, BuildPlan with grilling present also succeeds (NO_ERROR). So the control is stable.\n\nLet me structure it:\n\n```python\n# control: grilling present\nrc, out, err = build_and_run_probe(...)  # build + run\nif rc != 0: error \"probe crashed in control run\"\nelif 'NO_ERROR' not in out: error \"control run expected BuildPlan success, got ...\"\n```\n\nThen delete grilling, rebuild + run, assert grilling error.\n\nNow let me also handle: the probe needs env vars RICK_TASK10_RICK_DIR and RICK_TASK10_JOB_PLAN_DIR. I'll set them via env dict.\n\nLet me now also decide on binary build for normal/boundary: build to temp `rick_bin_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task10_bin_')`, `rick_bin = os.path.join(rick_bin_dir, 'rick')`. `go build -o rick_bin ./cmd/rick` cwd=repo_root.\n\nRun: `run([rick_bin, 'plan', '--dry-run'], cwd=repo_root)`.\n\nNow, let me also verify the dry-run output goes to stdout (yes, PlanDryRun uses fmt.Printf/Println to stdout).\n\nLet me also make sure the grep for `{{` is done on stdout (the prompt content). The output includes the \"[DRY-RUN] Plan prompt:\" header and prompt content. Both on stdout. Good.\n\nLet me write the final script now.\n\nOne more consideration: the script should compute line count as `len(stdout.splitlines())`. For the `{{` count, use `stdout.count('{{')`. For boundary, use `len(re.findall(r'Grilling|结构化追问', stdout))`.\n\nAlso, I should import `re`.\n\nLet me also think about timeouts: go build can take a while first time. Use timeout=300 for build, 120