s. Let me use os.Args:\n\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    rickDir := \".\"\n    jobPlanDir := \"\"\n    if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n        rickDir = os.Args[1]\n    }\n    if len(os.Args) > 2 {\n        jobPlanDir = os.Args[2]\n    }\n    _, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().BuildPlan(\"dry-run requirement\", map[string]string{\n        \"rick_dir\":     rickDir,\n        \"job_plan_dir\": jobPlanDir,\n    })\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThis is cleaner and avoids env manipulation. I'll run `[probe_bin, rick_dir, job_plan_dir]`.\n\nNow, let me finalize the probe Go code. Note: in the Python string, I need to escape backslashes properly. I'll use a triple-quoted string with `\\\\n` for newlines in format strings? Actually the Go code uses `fmt.Printf(\"ERR:%v\\\\n\", err)` — in Python triple-quoted string, `\\\\n` becomes `\\n` (literal backslash-n) in the written file, which is what Go needs (Go source `\\n` escape). Wait, let me be careful:\n\nIn Python source, `'''...fmt.Printf(\"ERR:%v\\\\n\", err)...'''` — the `\\\\n` in a regular (non-raw) Python string becomes `\\n` (backslash + n) in the actual string value, which when written to the .go file is `\\n` (backslash-n), which Go interprets as newline escape. Correct. This matches task9.py's approach (`\\\\n`).\n\nGood. Let me write everything.\n\nLet me also think about whether to print debug to stderr. I'll keep it minimal: no debug output needed. Maybe print nothing to stderr except on unexpected issues? The requirement says \"调试信息请输出到 stderr\". I won't emit debug info; I'll just emit the final JSON to stdout.\n\nNow let me write the file.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one thing about the normal path assertion and the possibility that the test should also check \"单个\" (single) — i.e., that there's ONE coherent prompt, not scattered files. The test method's operation is `wc -l` (lines > 0) and `grep -c '{{'` (== 0). The \"single file cohesion\" is really tested by boundary test 2 (grilling inlined). So test 1 is just: output exists and is a fully-rendered prompt (no placeholders). I'll implement exactly that.\n\nLet me now also decide: should the boundary test run the binary separately, or reuse the stdout from test 1? To be faithful to \"操作 = ./bin/rick plan --dry-run | grep ...\", I'll run it separately (fresh subprocess) so each test step is independent and clear. It's a bit slower but clearer. Actually, reusing the same captured stdout is fine and faster, but running separately is more faithful and isolates failures. I'll run separately to match the test method's two separate commands (wc -l and grep are two commands in test 1 too). \n\nActually, to be efficient and avoid running the binary 3+ times, I'll run once and reuse for test1 (lines + `{{`) and test2 (grilling). But the test method describes separate commands. Both are acceptable. Running twice (once for test1, once for test2) is cleaner for isolation. I'll run twice. The binary is fast.\n\nHmm, actually running once and reusing is totally fine and I'll do one run for test1 assertions and a second run for test2 to clearly separate. Let me just run twice — negligible cost.\n\nLet me write it now.\n\nLet me also make the error messages clear and informative (with tail of output).\n\nFinal script:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"task10 验收测试：pibuilder 产出单文件内聚的 pi 定制化规范产物。...\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\n\n_PROBE_GO = '''package main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/builder\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\trickDir := \".\"\n\tjobPlanDir := \"\"\n\tif len(os.Args) > 1 {\n\t\trickDir = os.Args[1]\n\t}\n\tif len(os.Args) > 2 {\n\t\tjobPlanDir = os.Args[2]\n\t}\n\t_, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().BuildPlan(\"dry-run requirement\", map[string]string{\n\t\t\"rick_dir\":     rickDir,\n\t\t\"job_plan_dir\": jobPlanDir,\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"ERR:%v\\\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tfmt.Println(\"NO_ERROR\")\n}\n'''\n\n\ndef find_repo_root(start_file):\n    d = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(start_file))\n    probe = d\n    while True:\n        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(probe, '.git')):\n            return probe\n        parent = os.path.dirname(probe)\n        if parent == probe:\n            break\n        probe = parent\n    for _ in range(6):\n        d = os.path.dirname(d)\n    return d\n\n\ndef run(cmd, cwd, timeout=300, env=None):\n    try:\n        p = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env)\n        return p.returncode, p.stdout, p.stderr\n    except FileNotFoundError as e:\n        return 127, '', str(e)\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:\n        out = e.stdout or ''\n        err = (e.stderr or '') + '\\n[timeout after %ds]' % timeout\n        return 124, out, err\n\n\ndef tail(text, n=1600):\n    if not text:\n        return ''\n    return text[-n:]\n\n\ndef write_file(path, content):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(content)\n\n\ndef read_bytes(path):\n    with open(path, 'rb') as f:\n        return f.read()\n\n\ndef write_bytes(path, content):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'wb') as f:\n        f.write(content)\n\n\ndef main():\n    errors = []\n\n    repo_root = find_repo_root(__file__)\n    go = shutil.which('go')\n    if not go:\n        print(json.dumps({'pass': False, 'errors': ['go toolchain not found in PATH']}))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    # ---- 前置：build 成功（产物落临时目录，不污染 bin/rick） ----\n    bin_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task10_bin_')\n    rick_bin = os.path.join(bin_dir, 'rick')\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'build', '-o', rick_bin, './cmd/rick'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=600)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('go build ./cmd/rick failed:\\n' + tail(err or out))\n        # 构建失败则后续 CLI 断言无法执行，直接输出结果\n        print(json.dumps({'pass': False, 'errors': errors}))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    # ---- 正常路径：单文件内聚 prompt（行数 > 0，{{ 计数 0） ----\n    rc, out, err = run([rick_bin, 'plan', '--dry-run'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=120)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('rick plan --dry-run exit=%d:\\n%s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        lines = len(out.splitlines())\n        if lines <= 0:\n            errors.append('plan --dry-run 输出行数 = %d, 应为 > 0（非单个连贯 prompt）' % lines)\n        brace_count = out.count('{{')\n        if brace_count != 0:\n            errors.append('plan --dry-run 输出含 %d 个未替换 `{{` 占位符（应内联并全部替换）' % brace_count)\n\n    # ---- 边界：grilling skill 内容内联进主产物 ----\n    rc, out, err = run([rick_bin, 'plan', '--dry-run'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=120)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('rick plan --dry-run (边界) exit=%d:\\n%s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        grilling_hits = len(re.findall(r'Grilling|结构化追问', out))\n        if grilling_hits < 1:\n            errors.append('plan --dry-run 输出未内联 grilling 内容（grep \"Grilling|结构化追问\" 计数 = %d, 应 ≥ 1）' % grilling_hits)\n\n    # ---- 异常：缺 skill 内联源（删除 grilling.md + 重建） ----\n    probe_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='.tmp_task10_probe_', dir=repo_root)\n    write_file(os.path.join(probe_dir, 'main.go'), _PROBE_GO)\n    probe_bin = os.path.join(probe_dir, 'probe')\n    grilling_path = os.path.join(repo_root, 'internal', 'prompt', 'templates', 'skills', 'grilling.md')\n\n    rick_dir = os.path.join(repo_root, '.rick')\n    job_plan_dir = os.path.join(rick_dir, 'jobs', 'job_N', 'plan')\n\n    # 控制运行：grilling 存在时 BuildPlan 应成功（验证 probe 可用）\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'build', '-o', probe_bin, '.'], cwd=probe_dir, timeout=600)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('probe go build (控制) failed:\\n' + tail(err or out))\n    else:\n        rc, out, err = run([probe_bin, rick_dir, job_plan_dir], cwd=repo_root, timeout=120)\n        if rc != 0:\n            errors.append('probe 控制运行 exit=%d（BuildPlan 在 grilling 存在时应成功）:\\n%s' % (rc, tail(err or out)