{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The test is idempotent and produces a consistent RED result. The output is a single line of valid JSON with `pass: false` and exit code 1.\n\nNow let me verify the self-check criteria from the prompt:\n\n\"测试质量自检（强制）\":\n- 输出 \"pass\": false → 符合预期，测试正确覆盖了待实现的功能 ✓\n\nThe RED phase is correctly demonstrated:\n1. Normal path passes (this is a baseline/regression guard, already satisfied).\n2. Boundary fails (grilling not inlined — the feature to implement).\n3. Exception fails (BuildPlan silently succeeds when grilling missing — the error-handling to implement).\n\nThis confirms the test correctly covers the feature to be implemented.\n\nLet me do a final review of the test script to make sure it fully implements all three test methods from the prompt:\n\n1. ✅ Normal path: `plan --dry-run`, wc -l (lines > 0), grep -c '{{' (== 0).\n2. ✅ Boundary: `plan --dry-run`, grep -cE 'Grilling|结构化追问' (≥1).\n3. ✅ Exception: delete grilling.md + rebuild, run PIBuilder.BuildPlan, error contains grilling (not panic, not silent).\n\nAll three implemented. JSON output format correct. Absolute paths used. try-except/finally for restore. Idempotent.\n\nI'm confident the test script is complete and correct. Let me provide a concise summary.\n\nActually, let me double-check one more subtle thing: the prompt says the test script path is `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task10.py`. I wrote it to exactly that path. ✓\n\nAlso I declared the skills at the start (\"I will use skill:tdd and skill:testing-anti-patterns for test generation.\"). ✓\n\nDone. Let me write a concise summary of what I did and the RED result."}}
